  "application_type_full": "Full planning permission",
  "description": "•\tReplace the failing RAAC roof deck with a lightweight, supported roof system incorporating laid-to-falls insulation and high-performance waterproofing.\n•\tNew windows. \n•\tUpgrade and replicate original parapet, capping, and coping details to preserve the visual detailing integrity of the Church.\n•\tIntroduce discreet surface water management improvements, reducing the risk of hidden leaks and long-term decay which threaten the heritage fabric.\n•\tReproduce significant internal features such as the V-grooved ceiling profile, maintaining the building’s distinctive architectural rhythm and aesthetic.\n•\tImprove roof drainage.  \n•\tDeliver all interventions in accordance with heritage best practice, achieving long-term stability, safety, and performance while ensuring the least possible harm to the Church’s historic and architectural significance.",
